"The introduction rule for product types tells us that elements of a product "
"type §0 are constructed by *pairing* elements of type §1 with elements of "
"type §2.\n"
"\n"
"Given an element §3 and an element §4 there is a corresponding element of "
"the product type §5 that is denoted by §6.\n"
"\n"
